`Tendsto (fun t => ∫ x, K x y t * singleFun z x ∂count) (𝓝[>] 0) (𝓝 (singleFun z y))`.
`∫ x, K x y t * singleFun z x ∂count = ∑ x, K x y t * singleFun z x = K z y t` (sum over x picks x=z).
So the limit is `singleFun z y = if z = y then 1 else 0`. Good; for `u t z = K z y t`, the initial limit is `c z = if z = y then 1 else 0` — the same for K₁ and K₂. 

